# Environment Configuration Template

# Copy this file to create your environment-specific configuration
# This is a template - actual environment variables are set in deployment platform

## Development
For local development:
- Backend URL: http://localhost:5000/api
- Automatically detected when running on localhost

## Production
Update the backend URL in js/api.js with your deployed backend:

```javascript
const API_CONFIG = {
    BASE_URL: isLocalhost 
        ? 'http://localhost:5000/api' 
        : 'https://YOUR-BACKEND-URL.onrender.com/api',
    TIMEOUT: 10000
};
```

## Backend Hosting Options

### Render
- URL format: https://your-app-name.onrender.com

### Railway
- URL format: https://your-app-name.up.railway.app

### Cyclic
- URL format: https://your-app-name.cyclic.app

### Heroku
- URL format: https://your-app-name.herokuapp.com

## Required Backend Environment Variables
These should be set in your backend hosting platform:

- MONGODB_URI=your_mongodb_atlas_connection_string
- JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key_here
- PORT=5000
- NODE_ENV=production

## CORS Configuration
Ensure your backend allows requests from your frontend domain:

```javascript
const corsOptions = {
  origin: [
    'http://localhost:3000',
    'https://your-frontend-url.vercel.app'
  ],
  credentials: true
};
```
